# CONTESTI E SCOPE — avvio gen395.
#
# Mondo, premessa, citazione e credenza riportata devono restare oggetti
# distinti e confrontabili. I fatti sono inventati e materializzati a runtime:
# il ratchet prova il kernel della KB, non rivendica ancora che ogni superficie
# NL produca da sola questi record.

[mock core]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test world_and_premise_remain_visible_as_distinct_views]
!assert context(penguin_story, hypothesis)
!assert proposition_signature(tweety_can_fly, tweety, can_fly, positive)
!assert proposition_signature(tweety_cannot_fly, tweety, can_fly, negative)
!assert holds_in(world, tweety_can_fly)
!assert holds_in(penguin_story, tweety_cannot_fly)
!assert source_of(tweety_cannot_fly, task_premise)
!assert confidence_of(tweety_cannot_fly, stipulated)
> what is the context kind for penguin_story?
< Hypothesis.
> what is the local belief for penguin_story?
< Tweety cannot fly.
> what is the inherited belief for penguin_story?
< Tweety can fly.
> what are the visible beliefs for penguin_story?
< Tweety cannot fly and tweety can fly.
> what is the context conflict for penguin_story?
< World.
> what is the proposition source for tweety_cannot_fly?
< Task premise.
> what is the proposition confidence for tweety_cannot_fly?
< Stipulated.

[test scope_policy_changes_without_deleting_other_contexts]
!assert frame_act_for_turn(turn_alpha, entailment_query)
> what is the relevant scope for turn_alpha?
< Penguin story.
!forget scope_kind_for_act(entailment_query, hypothesis)
> what is the relevant scope for turn_alpha?
<! Penguin story.
> what is the local belief for world?
< Tweety can fly.
!assert scope_kind_for_act(entailment_query, hypothesis)
> what is the relevant scope for turn_alpha?
< Penguin story.

[test quotation_and_reported_belief_do_not_become_speaker_commitment]
!assert context(alice_quote, quotation)
!assert context(alice_report, reported_belief)
> what is the commitment status for alice_quote?
< Attributed only.
> what is the commitment status for alice_report?
< Attributed only.

[test a_local_correction_does_not_erase_the_scope]
!assert context(correction_scope, hypothesis)
!assert holds_in(correction_scope, sky_is_green)
!assert holds_in(correction_scope, sky_is_blue)
!assert supersedes_in(correction_scope, sky_is_blue, sky_is_green)
> what is the local belief for correction_scope?
< Sky is blue.
!forget context(correction_scope, hypothesis)
> what is the local belief for correction_scope?
<! Sky is blue.
!assert context(correction_scope, hypothesis)
> what is the local belief for correction_scope?
< Sky is blue.
!forget supersedes_in(correction_scope, sky_is_blue, sky_is_green)
> what is the local belief for correction_scope?
< Sky is green and sky is blue.
